!MIDISynth
==========

A General MIDI SoundFont and a small MIDI file player for RISC OS 5.
Programs built with the midisynth library use the SoundFont in here to
play music, so you only need one copy on your computer.

Installing
----------
Copy !MIDISynth into !Boot.Resources (open !Boot, then Resources) so it
is set up every time you start the computer. You can also just
double-click it once before running a program that needs it.

It sets:

  MIDISynth$SoundFont   the SoundFont file programs should use

To use a different SoundFont, replace the file called SoundFont inside
!MIDISynth, or set MIDISynth$SoundFont to your own .sf2 or .sf3 file after
!MIDISynth has booted.

SF3 SoundFonts (compressed, as used by MuseScore) work too. They are
small to download but are decoded into memory when loaded: a 24 MB .sf3
can need 300-400 MB of memory, and takes a while to load.


Playing a MIDI file
-------------------
At the command line (F12, or a Task window):

  *MIDIPlay [-l] [-v volume] [-r rate] [-t] <MIDI file> [SoundFont]

  -l          loop the song
  -v volume   volume in percent (default 100)
  -r rate     sample rate (default 44100)
  -t          don't play: render the song as fast as possible and
              report how much processor time the music needs

Press Escape to stop.

Needs RISC OS 5 with the SharedSound, StreamManager and
SharedSoundBuffer modules (as supplied with current RISC OS 5 releases).

